# Table Plan

A seating chart planner that runs entirely in a single HTML file. No account, no
server, no upload — open it in a browser and everything happens on your own
computer. Drop in a guest list, let it seat everyone, drag people around, and
export a clean chart for your caterer, venue, or wedding party.

<!-- Swap in a real screenshot or GIF here before publishing. -->
<!-- ![Table Plan](docs/screenshot.png) -->

## What it does

- **Import a guest list** from a CSV (any RSVP site — Zola, The Knot, a Google
  Sheet) or a PDF. It auto-detects the name, title, household, and RSVP columns,
  and filters to just the guests who are attending.
- **Review and clean** the list in one pass — fix typos inline, remove
  duplicates, add anyone the file missed.
- **Lay out the room** with round, banquet, and sweetheart tables, then let
  **auto-fill** seat everyone at once while keeping households together.
- **Mark couples** so they're always seated at the same table — optional, and
  flagged in red if a pair ever ends up apart.
- **Edit freely** — drag names onto seats, swap guests, add or remove individual
  chairs, rotate and move tables, rename anything. Full undo (Ctrl/Cmd+Z).
- **Works on touch** — drag-and-drop works on iPad and phone, not just mouse.
- **Export** an immaculate PDF (by name or by table), a CSV, or printable place
  cards.
- **Save** your whole chart back into the HTML file. Reopen that file any time
  and you're right where you left off.

## Getting started

1. Download `seating-chart-planner.html`.
2. Open it in a modern browser — Chrome, Safari, Edge, or Firefox.
3. Drag in your guest list, or use the included `sample-guest-list.csv` to try it.

That's it. There's nothing to install.

## Files in this repo

| File | What it is |
|------|------------|
| `seating-chart-planner.html` | The entire app — this is the product. |
| `sample-guest-list.csv` | A realistic 87-row RSVP export to test with. |
| `sample-by-name.pdf` | Example of the exported guest directory. |
| `sample-by-table.pdf` | Example of the exported table plan. |
| `demo-script.md` | A video walkthrough script for a demo. |

## Privacy

Your guest list never leaves your device. The app reads your file in the browser
and keeps everything in memory; nothing is sent anywhere. The one exception is
importing a **PDF**, which loads a PDF-reading library from a public CDN the
first time — so the first PDF import needs an internet connection. CSV import,
and everything else, works fully offline. (Scanned PDFs aren't supported, since
there's no text to read.)

## Customizing it

Everything you'd want to rebrand lives in two places near the top of the file:

- A `BRAND` block in the script — name, tagline, footer, and an optional support
  URL that adds a Help button.
- A `:root` block in the `<style>` — the color palette and fonts.

Change those and the whole app re-skins. Nothing else needs touching.

## Browser support

Works in current versions of Chrome, Safari, Edge, and Firefox, on desktop and
tablet. PDF export uses the browser's built-in "Save as PDF" in the print
dialog.

